{"kind":"stack","id":"s-food-chains","title":"Food chains: producers, predators and prey","theme":{"background":"#f4f9f0","foreground":"#1d3a22","font":"Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Producer"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"A living thing that makes its own food using sunlight. Plants are producers."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-q","content":"In a food chain, what gives energy to all the other living things?"},{"type":"button","id":"c2-a","label":"The Sun","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}],"why":"Category: a source of energy. The Sun's light energy is taken in by plants and passed along the chain."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"The soil","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}],"why":"Pupils often think plants get their food from the soil, but soil gives water and minerals, not energy."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-c","label":"The rain","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}],"why":"Rain helps plants grow but does not give them energy; pupils may forget that sunlight is needed."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"In the chain grass → rabbit → fox, which animal is the prey?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"The rabbit","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}],"why":"Category: an animal that is eaten. The rabbit is eaten by the fox, so it is the prey."},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"The fox","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}],"why":"Pupils mix up predator and prey; the fox is the one doing the hunting, not the one being hunted."},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"The grass","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}],"why":"Grass is eaten, but it is a producer at the start of the chain, not the animal being hunted."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"Which living thing is a predator in the chain grass → mouse → owl?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"The owl","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}],"why":"Category: an animal that hunts others. The owl hunts the mouse, so it is the predator."},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"The mouse","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}],"why":"The mouse is the prey, which pupils often confuse with the predator because it is in the middle."},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"The grass","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}],"why":"Grass is a producer at the start of the chain and does not hunt anything."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"You are a rabbit in a meadow. A fox is coming. Do you run to the bushes or hide under a log?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Run to the bushes","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Hide under the log","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"You run fast through the bushes and escape the fox. You are safe for now."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"You hide under the log and stay very still. The fox sniffs around but moves on."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"Which word describes a plant in a food chain?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"Producer","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}],"why":"Category: a living thing in a food chain. Plants make their own food, so they are producers."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Predator","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}],"why":"Pupils may think any living thing in a chain is a predator, but predators only hunt other animals."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"Prey","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}],"why":"Prey is an animal that is eaten, and plants are not usually hunted in this way."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-t","content":"Predator"},{"type":"text","id":"c9-e","content":"An animal that hunts and eats other animals."},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"In the chain grass → rabbit → fox, what does the fox eat?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"The rabbit","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}],"why":"Category: an animal that is eaten. The fox eats the rabbit, so the rabbit is its food."},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"The grass","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}],"why":"Pupils may think the fox eats plants, but grass is eaten by the rabbit, not the fox."},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"The sun","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}],"why":"The Sun gives energy to the chain but is not a living thing that the fox could eat."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done! You finished the food chains lesson."},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"You now know how to find producers, predators and prey in a food chain. Keep looking at the living things around you."}],"actions":[]}}
